#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157065 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf6a3dbb-52b3-5384-b640-0fbf29a6cc98" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving a Cube Root"}] :question/id #uuid "813b7b5f-0da8-5a92-b4ff-f7208c5f059f" :question/math-academy-id "e-7654" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt[3]{x+3} + 1 \\geq 0$." :question/worked-solution "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt[3]{x + 3} + 1 & \\ge 0 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{x + 3} & \\ge - 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(\\sqrt[3]{x + 3})^{3} & \\ge (-1)^{3} \\\\ x + 3 & \\ge - 1 \\\\ x & \\ge - 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157066 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "24f2c5a5-dc56-5f78-8138-8f7b3a6280e2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving a Square Root Compared to a Negative Number"}] :question/id #uuid "bc44bc68-a615-5f25-b686-8a775fcac64c" :question/math-academy-id "e-7655" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $3\\sqrt{x-2} +7 \\geq 4$." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{x - 2} + 7 & \\ge 4 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{x - 2} & \\ge - 3 \\\\ \\sqrt{x - 2} & \\ge - 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHere, the square root is greater than a negative number $(-1)$, so any number we can substitute into the square root will satisfy the inequality. So, the solution is the domain of the square root.\n\nTo find the domain, we recall that the expression under the square root must be greater than or equal to $0{:}$\n\n$$\nx-2 \\geq 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad x \\geq 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\geq 2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157067 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9003081-7cf6-5a99-accf-6a69b65db47c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving a Square Root Compared to a Positive Number"}] :question/id #uuid "bca45b70-4e79-5baf-a4be-186366cebdd5" :question/math-academy-id "e-7656" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $7-\\sqrt{x+3} < 5$." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 - \\sqrt{x + 3} & < 5 \\\\ -\\sqrt{x + 3} & < - 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{x + 3} & > 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nIn this inequality, the square root is being compared to a non-negative number $(2)$. So, we can square both sides of the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}(\\sqrt{x + 3})^{2} & > 2^{2} \\\\ x + 3 & > 4 \\\\ x & > 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we must only keep the solutions that are in the domain of the square root. To find the domain of the square root, we recall that the argument of the square root must be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x + 3 & \\ge 0 \\\\ x & \\ge - 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nOur solution is $x > 1$, which can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\left(1,\\infty \\right)\n$$\n\nThe domain of the square root is\n\n$$\nx \\geq -3\n$$\n\nwhich can be expressed as $[MATH: \\left[-3,\\infty \\right).]$ To find the solutions that are in the domain of the square root, we take the intersection:\n\n$[MATH: \\left(1,\\infty \\right) \\cap \\left[-3,\\infty \\right) =\\left(1,\\infty\\right)]$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx \\in \\left(1,\\infty\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich can also be written as $x > 1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9003081-7cf6-5a99-accf-6a69b65db47c" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inequality Involving a Square Root Compared to a Positive Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83a6ae1d-653f-5cc2-a213-62be95607364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3} \\le x \\le \\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156245} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f791b9-0b41-5fd3-bbc8-19ac994d83fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x \\le - \\frac{1}{3}$ or $x \\le \\frac{8}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156246} {:answer/id #uuid "2d070ea2-0273-5a28-bde8-5efe7044cfcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156247} {:answer/id #uuid "324eb938-4568-596c-bab5-f48f39a53f19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\ge - \\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156248} {:answer/id #uuid "35053ab5-6428-54c9-86eb-7782a78c26aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x \\le \\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83a6ae1d-653f-5cc2-a213-62be95607364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3} \\le x \\le \\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156245} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee517260-8643-55f5-b902-214156fc4d73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186156244}] :question/id #uuid "fefb96f6-18f6-5055-9c5e-8d69e5bbce1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-87508" :question/problem "Solve the inequality $-2\\sqrt{3x + 1} + 1 \\ge - 5$."}]}
